# W10d, guest b (k2): takes the gate to stag0101; its automatic join of a's instance waits (the relay's test hold, a
# scene's stand-in) on the loading screen; a removes it there: "You were removed from a's instance." and the DISSOLVE
# into the lobby on its own story at once (never a's story: key item 4 is a's, not b's). At the gate again a's instance
# is no candidate (the removal bar): b's arrival makes an instance of its own.
campaign until stage=stagml11,control
idle until epoch>=@100
explore mate00 yes until mode=parked
log b waits for its join
idle until stage=stagml11,control fail key:4=1,stage=stag0101,epoch>=@300
log b home after the removal in the wait
idle until frames>=120 fail key:4=1
log own story at home
explore mate00 yes until stage=stag0101,control fail epoch>=@560
log b in stag0101 again
idle until frames>=240 fail key:4=1
log b on its own story there
disk 8 until stage=stagml11,control
log b home again
